# The Dockerfiles in infra/docker do `COPY . .` from the repo root: keep secrets, local data and build outputs out of the image.
# Secrets (only the example stays)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
# Local storage: outbox mails, uploaded files, the dev DB, binaries
.local
**/.local
infra/docker/data
# Installed and built in the image, never copied from a workstation
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.log
# Repo and tooling metadata
.git
.github
.claude
**/.DS_Store
